t_HRTV_or_DBV_pseudotyped_viruses_require_GlcCer_for_efficient_entry_/22278557", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p><b>A.</b> Diagram of replication-competent rVSV-DBV genome. <b>B.</b> Replication-competent rVSV-HRTV entry in SPTLC2-, UGCG- or UGT8-deficiency cells. Control and KO 293T cells were infected with replication-competent rVSV-HRTV for 16 hours, followed by flow cytometry. <b>C.</b> Rescue of replication-competent rVSV-HRTV entry in SPTLC2-, UGCG- or UGT8-deficiency cells. Control and UGCG-KO 293T cells were cultured in media supplemented with 50 \u03bcM DMSO or GlcCer for 24 hours, followed by infection with replication-competent rVSV-HRTV for 16 hours prior to flow cytometry assay. <b>D.</b> Replication-competent rVSV-DBV entry in SPTLC2-, UGCG- or UGT8-deficiency cells. <b>E.</b> Rescue of replication-competent rVSV-DBV entry in SPTLC2-, UGCG- or UGT8-deficiency cells. The experiments were performed similarly as described above.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 336956, "created_date": "2023-03-15T17:35:18Z", "modified_date": "2023-10-24T06:47:54Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["recombinant viruses pseudotyped", "potential therapeutic target", "group binding pocket", "glucose ceramide glucosyltransferase", "dabie bandavirus glycoprotein", "dabie bandavirus </", "borne zoonotic viruses", "early entry events", "glycosphingolipid biosynthesis pathway", "biophysical analyses showed", "dangerous viral pathogens", "recovered viral entry", "produces glccer resulted", "play essential roles", "heartland bandavirus </", "div >< p", "mediated membrane fusion", "galcer ), glucosylceramide", "viral entry", "viral fusion", "mutagenesis showed", "glccer glycosphingolipid", "viral lifecycle", "membrane st